<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01436#audience_id> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The intended audience for this meme is individuals who are familiar with internet dark humor, particularly those who understand and engage with absurdist or satirical content that juxtaposes trivial or harmless visuals with violent or tragic scenarios. The meme targets viewers who may be exposed to or interested in online communities that appreciate shock value and irony, even when the content is harmful. It is likely aimed at a general internet audience that may not be aware of the harmful stereotypes it perpetuates, or who may find the dark humor amusing despite its toxicity. The meme also implicitly targets those who are familiar with the term 'tard strength' as a derogatory stereotype, suggesting an audience that may have encountered or used such language in online spaces. The target community includes individuals who may be desensitized to violence or tragedy, or who may be seeking humor in taboo subjects, often found in meme culture and online forums."@en .
