_:n1aa1e0e4b6fe4fe2bea80f2d06da1e6db35 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n1aa1e0e4b6fe4fe2bea80f2d06da1e6db36 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01436#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a brightly colored frog perched on a pink object against a blurred green background, juxtaposed with text that reads: 'when the school shooter accidentally shoots the autistic kid but doesn't know that the tard strength makes him impervious to bullets.' The overall intent is to create dark humor by combining a harmless, visually appealing image of a frog with a violent and tragic scenario involving an autistic person. The meme relies on the absurdity of the situation — the frog's resilience being metaphorically equated to the fictional 'tard strength' of an autistic individual — to generate a comedic effect. This approach is harmful as it trivializes a serious and traumatic event, potentially normalizing or mocking the suffering of autistic individuals. The meme contains harmful content by reducing a deeply sensitive issue to a joke, which can be offensive and damaging to the autistic community. It also risks perpetuating stereotypes by implying that autism confers invulnerability to violence, which is not only medically inaccurate but also potentially dangerous as it may mislead viewers about the real-world experiences and vulnerabilities of autistic people. The meme's intent is to provoke laughter through shock value and absurd juxtaposition, but this comes at the cost of reinforcing harmful narratives and potentially causing emotional harm to its target audience."@en .
