_:n1aa1e0e4b6fe4fe2bea80f2d06da1e6db43 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01436#juxtaposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The act of placing two contrasting elements side by side to create a striking or humorous effect. The meme uses juxtaposition to contrast the harmless, visually appealing frog with the violent and tragic scenario described in the text, creating an absurd and darkly humorous effect."@en .
_:n1aa1e0e4b6fe4fe2bea80f2d06da1e6db21 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:n1aa1e0e4b6fe4fe2bea80f2d06da1e6db54 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01436#assertion_about_01436> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "assertion_about_01436"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01436#dark_humor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The emotion expressed is dark humor, derived from the absurd and jarring juxtaposition of a harmless, visually appealing frog with a violent and tragic scenario involving an autistic person. The humor is intended to provoke laughter through shock value and absurdity, but it is rooted in harmful content and stereotypes."@en .
