<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#verticallyAdjacentTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates above/below spatial adjacency between dimension instances in memes"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01436#dark_humor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A comedic style that derives humor from morbid, tragic, or taboo subjects. The meme uses dark humor to create a jarring and absurd contrast between the harmless frog image and the violent scenario described in the text, which is intended to provoke laughter at the expense of a serious issue."@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01436#stereotype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A widely held but oversimplified belief about a particular group of people. The meme relies on harmful stereotypes about autism and violence, implying that autistic people are invulnerable to harm, which is not only inaccurate but also potentially dangerous. This stereotype is used to create a comedic effect that is offensive and damaging."@en .
